<name>TAKAHASHI TATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAKAWA SHIGEKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAO TOMOHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIKAWA, JUNICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKUDA, SEIJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAGI, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI, TATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAKAWA, SHIGEKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAO, TOMOHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A controller for elevators, comprising an elevator hall (5) where a cage (12) stops and passengers get on and off the cage, an elevator shaft (10) in which the cage ascends and descends, a control console (17) for controlling stoppage, ascent and descent of the cage, the control console being so disposed in the elevator shaft as not to interfere with the ascent and descent of the cage, and a mechanism for drawing out the control console to the elevator hall. Accordingly, it is possible to make effective use of the space in the elevator shaft and to readily make use of the elevator hall, which is not used by passengers at the time of maintenance, for the maintenance work.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Un organe de commande pour ascenseurs, comprenant un hall d'ascenseur (5) dans lequel une cabine (12) s'arrête et dans laquelle des usagers montent et en descendent, une gaine (10) d'ascenseur dans laquelle la cabine monte et descend, une console de commande (17) pour commander l'arrêt, la montée et la descente de la cabine, la console de commande étant disposée dans la gaine de l'ascenseur, de sorte qu'elle ne gêne pas la montée et la descente de la cabine, et un mécanisme permettant de tirer la console de commande et de la sortir du hall d'ascenseur. Ainsi, il est possible d'utiliser de manière efficace l'espace dans la gaine d'ascenseur et d'utiliser facilement ledit hall, espace utilisé par les usagers au moment de l'entretien, pour les travaux d'entretien.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>